On another occasion, Amos and I wondered about the rate of divorce among professors in our university.
 We noticed that the question triggered a search of memory for divorced professors we knew or knew about, and that we judged the size of categories by the ease with which instances came to mind.
 We called this reliance on the ease of memory search the availability heuristic.
 In one of our studies, we asked participants to answer a simple question about words in a typical English text:Consider the letter K.
